  "notes": "POI: Blackpool Tower (158 m; Historic England 53.8159,-3.0552). Owner's point treated as take-off (seafront, ~100 m W of the tower). Home/POI ground_m = 10 m from the nearest land cell of the 90 m DEM (the take-off cell itself reads 0 m, i.e. sea). Approach starts ~350 m out over the beach/sea and climbs at <=14 deg to 108 m (DJI Fly height; 118 m above sea level, so <=120 m even over the beach at low tide), then an 80 m-radius orbit; camera tilted up at the upper tower (aim 130 m) so the crown is in frame. Tower is ~5.2 km (2.8 nm) from Blackpool Airport's reference point; its FRZ covers the seafront south of Central Pier."
